  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian and legal assistance to the victims of the Pando massacre</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On 11 September 2008, a group of 230 small farmers and indigenous people was violently attacked by an armed group in the Bolivian department of Pando, leaving 18 people killed &#x2013; including children &#x2013; and 51 still accounted for. This project aims to support a key CAFOD partner in Bolivia UNITAS and its member organisations CIPCA (another key CAFOD partner), CEJIS and IPHAE to 
1) Deal with the immediate humanitarian assistance to at least 70 refugees in the city of La Paz and an estimated 4000 people stuck in the area with a continued climate of fear, violence and impunity.
2) Provide urgent legal support to the families of those massacred, and those wounded. 3) Implement a communications and advocacy strategy to ensure a timely and correct legal process as well as contribute to the creation of safe conditions for returning refugees and those not daring to leave their houses.</narrative>
  </description>
